{# Field list (module spec §11.6) — rendered and managed client-side by
   /assets/js/news-form-builder.js from window.NEWS_EDITOR_DATA.fields
   (serialized back into fields_json on submit), since fields are saved
   together with the article in one POST rather than through their own
   AJAX endpoints (module spec §11.5: "Enregistrer... saves article + form
   definition in one POST"). The first field is always a pinned "bloc de
   texte" (usability review) — the JS never lets it be deleted or moved.
   The rest of the form's settings live in the separate
   partials/_form_settings.html.twig box, shown only once a real input
   field exists. #}
<div id="news-fields-list" class="d-flex flex-column gap-2 mb-2"></div>
<button type="button" class="btn btn-outline-secondary w-100" style="border-style:dashed;" id="news-add-field-btn">
    <i class="bi bi-plus-lg" aria-hidden="true"></i> Ajouter un champ
</button>
<div id="news-field-type-picker" class="d-none border rounded-3 p-3 mt-2">
    <div class="d-flex justify-content-between align-items-center mb-2">
        <span class="small text-body-secondary">Choisissez un type de champ</span>
        <button type="button" class="btn-close" id="news-field-picker-close" aria-label="Fermer"></button>
    </div>
    <div class="row g-2" id="news-field-type-grid"></div>
</div>
